    "parameters" : "patient",
    "sections" : [
      {
        "executes" : false,
        "heading" : "Contract",
        "line" : 19,
        "lines" : [
          "Input: a patient",
          "Output: either an immediate escalation or a recorded triage level chosen",
          "by a clinician",
          "Side effect: an escalation pages the on-call attending on the spot; a",
          "triage level gets attached to the patient's chart either way"
        ],
        "role" : "reference"
      },
      {
        "executes" : true,
        "heading" : "When to invoke",
        "line" : 26,
        "lines" : [
          "\"triage patient\"",
          "\"run patient triage\""
        ],
        "role" : "applicability"
      },
      {
        "executes" : true,
        "heading" : "Workflow",
        "line" : 30,
        "lines" : [
          "read the vital signs for the patient",
          "if any of the vital signs is critical,",
          "escalate the patient",
          "Emit: \"triage patient escalated\"",
          "if not any of the vital signs is critical,",
          "use judgment to weigh every vital sign against its own ceiling and recommend a triage level",
          "ask the user to choose between \"admit\", \"observe\", \"discharge\"",
          "Emit: \"triage patient pass complete\""
        ],
        "role" : "procedure"
      },
      {
        "executes" : false,
        "heading" : "Anti-Patterns",
        "line" : 40,
        "lines" : [
          "Don't wait for a second critical reading to confirm the first — a single",
          "vital sign past its ceiling is already the escalation trigger, not a",
          "suggestion to recheck first",
          "Don't let the judgment call second-guess a critical vital sign that",
          "already fired the escalation branch; the two paths are mutually",
          "exclusive by design, not a fallback chain"
        ],
        "role" : "reference"
      },
      {
        "executes" : false,
        "heading" : "When NOT to use this skill",
        "line" : 48,
        "lines" : [
          "Use `vitals monitor` instead for the recurring background check that keeps",
          "watching a patient between triage passes — this skill is a single point-in",
          "-time decision, not the ongoing watch. Use `medication administer` once a",
          "triage level has already produced an order that needs to be given"
        ],
        "role" : "reference"
      },
      {
        "executes" : false,
        "heading" : "Report shape",
        "line" : 54,
        "lines" : [
          "The receipt records which branch fired — an immediate escalation or a",
          "human-chosen triage level — and the level itself when a human made the",
          "call"
        ],
        "role" : "template"
      }
    ],
    "triggers" : "\"triage patient\"\n\"run patient triage\""
  },
